[h2]Figures & quotes[/h2]
[img src=static/bubbles.svg width=40 alt="bloops logo" caption="Rendered from an img tag"][/img]
[asy src=static/triangle.svg label=triangle width=45 alt="A triangle" caption="Compiled from an asy block"]
size(6cm);
pen fg = rgb("cdd6f4");
pair A = (0, 0), B = (4, 0), C = (1.2, 3), O = (2, 0.94);
draw(A--B--C--cycle, fg + linewidth(0.8));
draw(circle(O, abs(O - A)), rgb("89b4fa") + linewidth(0.8));
dot("$A$", A, SW, rgb("cba6f7"));
dot("$B$", B, SE, rgb("cba6f7"));
dot("$C$", C, N, rgb("cba6f7"));
[/asy]
[quote author="Paul Erdős" link="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Erd%C5%91s"]
A mathematician is a device for turning coffee into theorems.
[/quote]

[h2]Math boxes[/h2]
[theorem title=Pythagoras]
In a right triangle, $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$.
[/theorem]
[proof]
Rearrange four copies of the triangle inside a square of side $a + b$.
[/proof]
[lemma]Every tree with $n$ vertices has $n - 1$ edges.[/lemma]
[proposition]$\sqrt{2}$ is irrational.[/proposition]
[corollary title="of the lemma"]A forest with $c$ components has $n - c$ edges.[/corollary]
[example]$3, 10, 5, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1$ is a Collatz sequence.[/example]
[claim title=key]The sum of two odd numbers is even.[/claim]
[exercise]Show that $n^3 - n$ is divisible by $6$.[/exercise]
[problem title="AMC-style"]Find the remainder when $2^{10}$ is divided by $7$.[/problem]
[hide label="Click to reveal the solution"]
[soln]
Since $2^3 \equiv 1 \pmod 7$, we get $2^{10} = (2^3)^3 \cdot 2 \equiv 2$.
[/soln]
[/hide]
